cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EXBYCost, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software

title: "EXBYCost: a techno-economic modeling tool for estimating extraction costs from food processing byproducts"
abstract: >-
  EXBYCost is a techno-economic analysis (TEA) tool for
  estimating the cost of extracting valuable compounds from food processing
  byproducts. Built on the BioSTEAM process simulation framework and delivered
  as an interactive Streamlit web application, it simulates a complete
  solid-liquid extraction process, including feedstock drying and milling,
  solvent extraction, solvent recovery by multi-effect evaporation with
  recycle, and product drying without the need for adding extra experimental data
  It reports the capital cost breakdown, annual
  operating costs, stream and mass balance information, and the minimum
  product selling price, together with its cost contributions. EXBYCost also
  supports parameter sweeps and sensitivity analysis of the minimum selling
  price, and flags compounds at risk of thermal degradation under the
  selected process conditions.

